{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>A bell and a pomegranate.</b> It was necessary to write this, lest you think it is possible to make two or three bells inside two or three pomegranates and call them ״inside the pomegranates.״ Therefore it says <b>a bell and a pomegranate</b> — meaning, he should not make two bells with a pomegranate. And it returned to say <b>a bell and a pomegranate</b> a second time to preclude that he not make two pomegranates for each bell, so that each bell is within two pomegranates, nor that you raise the pomegranate on the right of this bell to the left of the bell that follows it. Therefore it said a second time <b>a bell and a pomegranate</b> — meaning, adjacent to the pomegranate of the first bell will be the second bell. Understand:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:14.300194217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}